@@ -4,23 +4,24 @@ info:
   title: DSP Support - Password API
   description: |
     Internal CM password setup/reset. CM validates user entitlement and the approved one-time Code.
-    Only the configured CM APIC subscription is accepted; Channel alone is not authorization.
-    Deploy with dsp.password.cm-client-id/secret set to the existing BM DSP subscription (DSP.APIC_CLIENT_ID/SECRET in CM).
+    Internal APIC authenticates and authorizes the CM subscription before routing to DSP.
+    DSP password services do not revalidate APIC client credentials or require a duplicate credential configuration.
     A creates a password; M replaces an existing active password without an old password.
     Password hash format is Base64(raw SHA-256(UTF-8(password))), stored without rehashing.
     OAEP SHA-256, MGF1 SHA-256, empty label; encrypted bytes use Base64.
 
     ---
     ### Global Required Headers
-    To ensure API security and traceability, all requests must include the following headers.
+    The following headers describe requests from CM to internal APIC. APIC validates its client credentials;
+    DSP uses the existing shared header processing for Message-Id and Channel.
 
     | Header Name | Type | Mandatory(M) / Optional(O) | Description | Example |
     | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
     | **Message-Id** | `string` | **M** | Message ID. Must comply with UUID v4 format. Constant "Server-Define" will lead to UUID generated by HTH system. | `1f0ee48b-ce99-475f-8b72-52a7a492edfa` or `Server-Define` |
     | **Authorization** | `string` | **O** | The access token is returned in logon API. The token includes user closed ID by DSP. | `Bearer eyJhbG...` |
-    | **Channel** | `string` | **M** | Distinguish channel (HTH, BCO, BCM). Corporate hardcode 'HTH'. | `HTH` |
-    | **X-IBM-Client-Id** | `string` | **M** | APIC client ID. Corporate retrieves the info when onboarding. | `client-id-12345` |
-    | **X-IBM-Client-Secret** | `string` | **M** | APIC secret. Corporate retrieves the info when onboarding. | `client-secret-abcde` |
+    | **Channel** | `string` | **M** | Distinguish channel (HTH, BCO, BCM). CM sends 'BCO'. | `BCO` |
+    | **X-IBM-Client-Id** | `string` | **M** | Internal APIC caller ID, validated by APIC. Reuses the existing BM DSP subscription. | `client-id-12345` |
+    | **X-IBM-Client-Secret** | `string` | **M** | Internal APIC caller secret, validated by APIC. Not a DSP password-service configuration. | `client-secret-abcde` |
 
     ---
   version: "1.0.0"
